cast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Nevada enters the 2028 presidential race as one of the closest states on the map. The state's partisan lean is roughly even, tilting Republican by about a point, and with a term-limited incumbent president stepping away, neither party starts with an incumbency edge. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying fundamentals.\n\nRecent headlines have focused on Democratic primary politics rather than the general election: the party's new 2028 calendar moved Nevada out of its first-in-the-nation slot, and early primary voters are divided on issues like aid to Israel. Those stories shape the nomination fight more than the November matchup. Until credible statewide polling or ratings arrive, Nevada looks like a genuine tossup with a slight Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4561, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4622, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4628, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4646, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4672, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4612, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4728, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4601, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4654, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4647, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4638, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.469, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4636, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.46, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4592, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4612, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4555, "margin": -1.0}, 